{title: Jesus, Thou Joy of Loving Hearts}
{artist: Bernard of Clairvaux, tr. Ray Palmer / Henry Baker}
{genre: Hymn, Communion}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: F}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Book of Hymns (Nashville, Tennessee: United Methodist Publishing House, 1966), # 270)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Jesus, Thou Joy of [Gm]lov[C]ing [F]hearts,
[F]Thou Fount of [Gm]life, [C]Thou [F]Light of [C]men,
[C]From the best [G7]bliss that earth im[C]parts,
[F7]We turn un[Bb]filled to [C7]Thee a[F]gain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Thy truth unchanged hath [Gm]ev[C]er [F]stood;
[F]Thou savest [Gm]those [C]that [F]on Thee [C]call;
[C]To them that [G7]seek Thee Thou art [C]good,
[F7]To them that [Bb]find Thee [C7]all in [F]all.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]We taste Thee, O Thou [Gm]liv[C]ing [F]Bread,
[F]And long to [Gm]feast [C]up[F]on Thee [C]still;
[C]We drink of [G7]Thee, the Fountain[C]head,
[F7]And thirst our [Bb]souls from [C7]Thee to [F]fill.
{end_of_verse}
